1
00:00:00,870 --> 00:00:05,130
Valmiki cursed a
hunter in anger…

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,570
and that curse…

3
00:00:06,570 --> 00:00:08,373
became the Ramayana.

4
00:00:09,283 --> 00:00:11,583
This Valmiki Jayanti story…

5
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:13,719
is about pain and anger.

6
00:00:14,449 --> 00:00:16,359
Dawn on the Tamasa river…

7
00:00:16,359 --> 00:00:19,622
a pair of krauncha
birds sing in a tree.

8
00:00:19,622 --> 00:00:24,744
Then… an arrow. The male bird
falls… his mate keeps crying.

9
00:00:24,764 --> 00:00:26,554
Valmiki cries out—

10
00:00:26,554 --> 00:00:29,276
'Hunter, may you
never find peace!'

11
00:00:29,486 --> 00:00:31,046
Then he stops…

12
00:00:31,046 --> 00:00:34,903
'What did I say?' Angry words…
yet in rhythm!

13
00:00:35,313 --> 00:00:38,263
Valmiki said— 'This was born
of grief, shoka…

14
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:40,953
so let it be called a shloka.'

15
00:00:41,423 --> 00:00:46,651
Hunter, may you find no rest
for endless years…

16
00:00:46,651 --> 00:00:51,701
for you killed one of a pair
lost in love.

17
00:00:52,671 --> 00:00:55,162
It means: 'Hunter, may you
find no rest…

18
00:00:55,162 --> 00:00:57,903
you killed one bird of a
loving pair.'

19
00:00:58,343 --> 00:01:01,973
Nishada means hunter. Then
Brahma said—

20
00:01:01,973 --> 00:01:04,117
'Tell Rama's story
in this metre.'

21
00:01:04,327 --> 00:01:06,527
It could have stayed a curse…

22
00:01:06,527 --> 00:01:07,957
but Valmiki paused…

23
00:01:07,957 --> 00:01:10,230
and the pain became poetry.

24
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:12,390
So today, when
something hurts…

25
00:01:12,390 --> 00:01:15,422
before you reply,
write four lines.

26
00:01:16,052 --> 00:01:19,112
What did your pain turn into?
Comment below…

27
00:01:19,112 --> 00:01:21,503
A curse became the Ramayana.
